{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:3906-1","published":"2026-09-01T09:10:15Z","modified":"2026-09-10T18:23:19.871951621Z","related":["CVE-2026-54284","CVE-2026-59893","CVE-2026-59894","CVE-2026-71491"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-54284","CVE-2026-59893","CVE-2026-59894","CVE-2026-71491"],"summary":"Security update for python3-sqlparse","details":"This update for python3-sqlparse fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-54284: high algorithm complexity when parsing SQL payloads with hundreds of nesting levels can lead to denial\n  of service via excessive resource consumption (bsc#1275459).\n- CVE-2026-59893: quadratic complexity when processing unmatched dollar-quoted literal and multiline-comment delimiters\n  can lead to denial of service (bsc#1275461).\n- CVE-2026-59894: improper backlash escaping allows for injection of Python or PHP code via a crafted SQL input\n  (bsc#1275460).\n- CVE-2026-71491: quadratic complexity in `group_comments` when processing comment-only statements can lead to denial\n  of services (bsc#1275466).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"python3-sqlparse","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Module for Basesystem 15 SP7","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python3-sqlparse&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Module%20for%20Basesystem%2015%20SP7"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.4.2-150300.23.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"python3-sqlparse":"0.4.2-150300.23.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:3906-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"python3-sqlparse","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-ESPOS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/python3-sqlparse&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-ESPOS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.4.2-150300.23.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"python3-sqlparse":"0.4.2-150300.23.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https:/